      "synthesis": {
        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "All complexes 1–5 were prepared analogously. To a stirred solution of LH4 (0.046 g, 0.12 mmol) in methanol (20 mL) was added Ln(NO3)3·5H2O (0.24 mmol), giving a yellow solution that was stirred for 10 min. Triethylamine (0.09 mL, 0.6 mmol) was added dropwise at room temperature and stirring continued for 15 min. Pivalic acid (0.025 g, 0.24 mmol) was then added and stirring continued for 12 h, yielding a yellow precipitate. The solid was filtered, washed with diethyl ether (2 × 20 mL), dried, redissolved in 1:1 methanol/chloroform, and crystallized by slow evaporation; yellow block crystals formed within a week. For 1: LH4 (0.046 g, 0.12 mmol), Dy(NO3)3·5H2O (0.107 g, 0.24 mmol), Et3N (0.09 mL, 0.6 mmol), PivH (0.025 g, 0.24 mmol).",
